config BR2_PACKAGE_LIVI_APPLIANCE
    bool "LIVI appliance services"
    depends on BR2_aarch64
    depends on BR2_INIT_SYSTEMD
    depends on BR2_USE_MMU
    depends on BR2_TOOLCHAIN_HAS_THREADS
    depends on BR2_TOOLCHAIN_USES_GLIBC
    select BR2_PACKAGE_LIVI_LITE
    select BR2_PACKAGE_RAWLINK
    select BR2_PACKAGE_WESTON_TOUCH
    select BR2_PACKAGE_WESTON
    select BR2_PACKAGE_WESTON_HEADLESS
    select BR2_PACKAGE_WESTON_SHELL_KIOSK
    select BR2_PACKAGE_BASH
    select BR2_PACKAGE_BLUEZ5_UTILS
    # bluetoothctl: livi-core's package probe looks for it; the helper itself
    # talks to BlueZ over D-Bus.
    select BR2_PACKAGE_BLUEZ5_UTILS_CLIENT
    select BR2_PACKAGE_DBUS
    # avahi: the helper publishes and browses CarPlay's mDNS records through
    # avahi-publish-service/avahi-browse, which need the daemon running.
    select BR2_PACKAGE_AVAHI
    select BR2_PACKAGE_AVAHI_DAEMON
    select BR2_PACKAGE_HOSTAPD
    select BR2_PACKAGE_DNSMASQ
    select BR2_PACKAGE_IW
    select BR2_PACKAGE_WIRELESS_REGDB
    select BR2_PACKAGE_IPROUTE2
    select BR2_PACKAGE_UTIL_LINUX
    select BR2_PACKAGE_UTIL_LINUX_RFKILL
    select BR2_PACKAGE_ALSA_UTILS
    select BR2_PACKAGE_ALSA_UTILS_APLAY
    select BR2_PACKAGE_PULSEAUDIO
    select BR2_PACKAGE_PULSEAUDIO_DAEMON
    select BR2_PACKAGE_HOST_MTOOLS
    select BR2_PACKAGE_HOST_DOSFSTOOLS
    select BR2_PACKAGE_HOST_E2FSPROGS
    select BR2_PACKAGE_HOST_GENIMAGE
    help
      The systemd units, helper shims and first-boot state handling that turn
      the rawlink/weston/LIVI packages into the appliance: gadget-first boot
      order, a read-only rootfs with a small persistent /data partition,
      PulseAudio with a null-sink fallback, and the tiny sudo/nmcli shims the
      bundled python helper expects on a system without NetworkManager.

if BR2_PACKAGE_LIVI_APPLIANCE

config BR2_PACKAGE_LIVI_APPLIANCE_DEBUG
    bool "debug image (serial console, initcall_debug, dropbear)"
    help
      The release image has no serial console and no login. The debug image
      keeps the UART, boots with initcall_debug and loglevel=7 (which
      scripts/boottime.sh parses), adds dropbear, and leaves kernel tracing
      enabled. It is measurably slower; never ship it.

config BR2_PACKAGE_LIVI_APPLIANCE_GPU
    bool "H616 GPU and video engine (panfrost + cedrus)"
    help
      Load the board's accelerator modules at boot: on the Orange Pi Zero
      2W that is the H616 video engine (sunxi-cedrus) and the Mali-G31
      (panfrost), whose device tree nodes and power domains come from the
      board kernel-patches backports. The weston session then picks the GL
      renderer, livi-compositor's EGL binds the GPU and a hardware-decoded
      frame reaches it as a dmabuf without a copy.

      With the GPU, GStreamer has the v4l2 stateless decoders
      (v4l2slh264dec/v4l2slh265dec via gst1-plugins-bad) and LIVI decodes
      the phone's H.264/HEVC in hardware; Mesa panfrost (plus the
      OpenCL/CLC precompiler it requires) is enabled in the board
      defconfigs. Without a render node LIVI falls back to converting the
      decoder's frames to system memory for the software sink.

      The qemu image has neither device and leaves this off.

endif
